<title>CONGO: Italians to revive coffee, rubber plantation.</title>
<headline>Italians to revive coffee, rubber plantation.</headline>
<dateline>BRAZZAVILLE 1996-09-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>An Italian company plans to revive a coffee and a rubber plantation in the Mbila region of southwest Congo, Congolese officials said on Saturday.</p>
<p>Senior executives of the agro-industry firm Afrimex visited the plantations that were set up under French colonial rule in the 1950s about 400 km (300 miles) southwest of the capital Brazzaville.</p>
<p>An 800-hectare plantation produced 200 tonnes of rubber in the 1960s. A further 200 hectares were devoted to coffee production.</p>
<p>The project will create an estimated 500 jobs in the region where several timber companies already operate.</p>
</text>
